    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>One-to-one mapping between source and target values.</para><para>This container holds a one-to-one mapping from values in a domain to values in a range and can look up values in the forward or reverse direction in log time. It does so by consistently maintaining two maps: a forward map and a reverse map. The forward map maps values in the domain to values in the range, while the reverse map goes the other direction. The <ref refid="classSawyer_1_1Container_1_1BiMap_1af9ce6bab517123404badc458e471f5dc" kindref="member">forward</ref> and <ref refid="classSawyer_1_1Container_1_1BiMap_1a5533f42c7010eaa0624125d09118c213" kindref="member">reverse</ref> methods return const references to these maps. The <ref refid="classSawyer_1_1Container_1_1BiMap" kindref="compound">BiMap</ref> container provides methods for modifying the mapping. </para>    </detaileddescription>
